{"name":"Cape Hope","hex":"#d8d6d7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece or point of land, extending beyond the adjacent coast into a sea or lake; a promontory; a headland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sleeveless garment or part of a garment, hanging from the neck over the back, arms, and shoulders.","A superhero."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cape"},{"term":"hope","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To want (something) to happen, with a sense of expectation that it might .mw-parser-output .object-usage-tag{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output .deprecated{color:var(--wikt-palette-grey-lime-8,olivedrab)}[with that (+ clause); or  with clause; or with so or  not].","To intend to do something and look forward to the prospect of having done it [with to (+ infinitive)]."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The feeling of trust, confidence, belief or expectation that something wished for can or will happen.","The actual thing wished for."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hope"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cape Hope","blocks":[{"text":"Cape Hope is a headland in the Scoresby Sound, east Greenland, Sermersooq municipality."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Cape_hope_scoresby.jpg/330px-Cape_hope_scoresby.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape_Hope","wikidata":"Q24831125"},{"title":"Cape","blocks":[{"text":"A cape is a clothing accessory or a sleeveless outer garment of any length that hangs loosely and connects either at the neck or shoulders. They usually cover the back, shoulders, and arms. They come in a variety of styles and have been used throughout history for many different reasons."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape","wikidata":"Q1034198"},{"title":"Hope","blocks":[{"text":"Hope is an optimistic state of mind that is based o